# Castlevania: Legacy of Darkness (US) seeds of Archipelago's CVLoD world. No decomp:
# everything is placed by address. Same Konami engine as CV64, but relinked -- the
# addresses are LoD's own, found individually, not CV64's plus an offset.
#
# The stub goes in the dead debug block at 0x8001E4E0-0x8001EB30 (0x650 bytes, the same
# size as CV64's processMeter block), which nothing in the 16 MiB references. Archipelago's
# own patch puts its boot stub in the front of that block, ending at 0x8001E7E2, so ours
# sits at the far end and leaves AP 0x1DC bytes to grow into before the two would meet.
STUB_VRAM=0x8001E9C0
STUB_MAX=368
# Measured during play with tools/ram-usage.lua: 10 minutes, 595 samples, base RAM settled
# at 848/1024 pages by minute four and never moved after. The tool reports the whole
# Expansion Pak untouched, which is not believed: LoD points the VI at framebuffers at
# 0x80640000, 0x806D0000 and 0x8076E000, and the RDP writes those, so BizHawk's GLideN64
# never shows them. Everything from 0x80640000 up is therefore treated as occupied. Below
# it, Archipelago's own payload ends at 0x80400000 -- the measurement confirms itself here,
# its largest base-RAM free run stopping dead at 0x803F8000 where that payload loads. No
# lui+immediate pair anywhere in the ROM, retail or patched, forms an address in
# 0x80470000-0x80498000.
AGENT_VRAM=0x80480000
AGENT_ROM=0x1000000
AGENT_MIN_RAM=0x800000
